+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable-5-1/1.0", at: 2026-09-29T13:55:29.311Z }
+---
+
+# Community moderation of comments
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment on posts, and no moderator is on call. One bad actor
+must not be able to fill a post with spam, and one annoyed reader must not
+be able to silence a comment alone.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user may comment on any post and report any comment.
+- A comment is deleted for real (no soft delete) by its author or by the
+  author of the post it is on; nobody else
+  ([CommentPolicy](../../app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts)).
+- A report is one `comment_reports` row per (comment, user); the unique index
+  on that pair makes a repeated report a no-op.
+- A comment with `COMMENT_HIDE_THRESHOLD` (3) or more reports is left out of
+  the post page for every viewer, its author and the post's author included.
+  The row stays in `comments` for later review.
+- Deleting a post or a comment deletes the dependent comments and reports in
+  the application, inside one transaction. The foreign keys also declare
+  `ON DELETE CASCADE`, but SQLite only honours it on a connection with
+  `foreign_keys` switched on, which the default connection does not do.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Three colluding accounts can hide any comment. A review screen that
+  restores or removes hidden comments is the planned counterweight and is
+  not built yet.
+- Hidden comments are invisible to their authors too, without notice.
+- The post page counts reports on every view; the count is one grouped
+  query per page, bounded by the post's comments.
